                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- LEFT COLUMN -->
        <div class="card" style="border-top-color: #d97706;">
            <h2 class="card-title" style="color: #d97706; border-bottom-color: #fef3c7;">Dominant Downside Risks</h2>

            <div class="highlight-box">
                <div class="highlight-text">RISK BALANCE:<br>Tilted to the Downside</div>
                <div class="highlight-sub">A consistent, alarming finding across all eight editions.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="text-body">
                <p>The persistence of the narrow growth band is overshadowed by compounding vulnerabilities:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Trade Policy Escalation:</strong> Surges in tariffs and retaliatory measures, especially from 2025 onward. Front-loading of activity temporarily masked the underlying damage.</li>
                    <li><strong>Geopolitical Tensions:</strong> Deepening conflicts in the Middle East and broader security concerns, escalating sharply by the "Shadow of War" (Apr 2026) edition.</li>
                    <li><strong>Technology Re-evaluation:</strong> Growing fears that elevated expectations and investments around Artificial Intelligence could face a sudden market correction.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <h2 class="card-title" style="margin-top: 40px;">Inflation & Monetary Dynamics</h2>
            <div class="text-body">
                <p>While global headline inflation has been on a declining trajectory enabling a late-2024 "policy pivot," the path remains uneven:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>The US Exception:</strong> US inflation is projected to remain above target longer than in peer economies.</li>
                    <li><strong>Sticky Services:</strong> Persistent services inflation has slowed the broader disinflation process globally.</li>
                    <li><strong>Renewed Pressures:</strong> By April 2026, new inflationary pressures emerged linked to defense spending and supply chain fractures.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- RIGHT COLUMN -->
